  "scoringNotes": [
    "Score = 100 x (sum of eligible weights - deductions) / sum of eligible weights. A category is eligible only when it has at least one base rule with penalty > 0 AND at least one of its base checks produced evidence (pass or finding); otherwise it is reported as excluded and contributes no points.",
    "A proven critical storage failure (Windows HealthStatus 'Unhealthy' or SMART PredictFailure=true, base rules only) sets riskLevel 'critical' and caps the score at riskGates.critical.scoreCap. riskLevel is independent from score status (availability) and from confidence (data quality).",
    "Only findings with state 'finding' and penalty > 0 reduce the score.",
    "Penalties are capped per category at its weight; 'unknown', 'access_denied', 'unsupported', 'not_collected' and 'error' states never reduce the score.",
    "Rules sharing a dedupeGroup count only once (highest penalty in the group).",
    "The base metric uses exactly the rules whose modes include 'simple', in both audit modes. Full-mode-only rules are analysis-only (penalty 0).",
    "Informative findings never penalize.",
    "Severity scale (FMP-05): info < attention < review_recommended. Inside one dedupeGroup the rule with the higher penalty never has a lower severity, so the visual priority never contradicts the score; ties are broken by penalty. perf.cpu_sustained_high keeps its id for compatibility but is an informative observation about a ~4 s sample (FMP-07)."
  ],
